# FIXED 2026-08-27 (the review's finding C, BUGS.md sec 16): this
# file now vets as its `expected` line says it should. Kept as the
# regression guard; the shared rows are vet-sizing-* and
# vet-must-over-a-container-* in test/spec/vet.tsv.
#
# C5 (use-cases 05, 06, 10): the same early fold in the other direction:
# length(min(1)) beside a spread template counts the schema's own
# spread-only (zero-member) container and refuses the SCHEMA, even
# though the data supplies a satisfying entry.
# expected: verdict: valid, exit 0 (data has one entry, min(1) holds)
# actual: verdict: error, exit 4 -- "the schema is unusable on its own":
#         $.x: constraint [conflict] expected length(integer&min(1))
#         actual {&:{"r":integer}}. Same shape with the data in the SAME
#         document (x: length(min(1)) & {&:{r:integer}} \n x: {a:{r:1}})
#         evaluates fine, and the list form ([&:string] & length(min(1)))
#         fails identically (use-case 06 probes/length-on-schema-list.aon,
#         10 gaps/list-length-template.aon).
# run: aontu vet sizing-min-kills-schema.aon one-entry.json
x: length(min(1)) & { &: {r: integer} }
